<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p28_do_slt_air_supply_sv)OTE(p00_io_winder:4:O.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder E-stop / rope switch device - 4:O.5

On when the winder E-stop is pressed or rope pull switch 4 is pulled:

  p00_io_winder:6:I.12  -> p01_di_winder_estop_active
  Local:5:I.Data.11     -> p01_di_rope_sw_4_active

Believed to be the alarm horn.  The program does not name it and the
drawing shows only the rev H reassignment, so confirm at the panel.

This is the original pre-accumulator function of 4:O.5.  Drawing DZ1615
rev H reassigned A-5 to the accumulator nip solenoid and the rung was
deleted with it.  Reinstated by request: the indicator keeps 4:O.5 and
the nip moves to 4:O.8, the first spare on that module (A-8, 1765-330).

NOTE: the program now differs from DZ1615 rev H sheet 5.  The drawing
needs revising - nip solenoid on A-8, not A-5.

Rev 20260904 a42]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p00_io_winder:6:I.12) ,XIC(Local:5:I.Data.11) ]OTE(p00_io_winder:4:O.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
