<![CDATA[OTE(p29r06.comment.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ultrasonic roll diameter sensor removed from service

The customer no longer uses it, so everything it fed is gone:

  - SYS_SCP from p00_io_winder:2:I.Ch5Data       channel now spare
  - the radius/diameter calculation
  - the two snap-up rungs that, on index complete, overwrote the
    calculated diameter with the sensor reading if it read larger

Those last two were LIVE, not dead - p29r20_index_complete is written
by the prox state machine - so with no sensor on the channel they were
free to corrupt a good calculated diameter on every index.

Diameter is unaffected: it comes from line speed / winder RPM in p29r17
and p29r18, and is only trusted while the tension loop is in band.

p29_ai_wdr_dia_in is left DECLARED so any HMI screen still referencing
it resolves.  It now reads 0 instead of a stale value.

Rev 20260904 a39]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,p29_ai_wdr_dia_in)MOV(0,p29_real_to_hmi[0])MOV(p29r06_ave_wdr_lc,p29_real_to_hmi[1])MOV(0,p29_real_to_hmi[2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
