<Routine Name="R11_Winder_B_Speed_Control" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[p29r10
This routine is called, continuously, from p29r01 Main while the plc is in Run mode.  All modes and fault reset requests are controlled, here.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()OTE(p29r11.comment.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tag Usage

p29r10.comment (dint)
p29r10.oneshot (dint)
p29r10_timer_xxxx (timer)
p29r10_xxxx (any)
p29r10.fault (dint)
p29r10.warning (dint)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(p29r11.fault,0)OTE(p29r11_run_permissive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Requests]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r11_run_permissive)[XIC(p01r13_line_running) ,XIC(p01r13_line_slow_ramp) ]XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active)XIC(p29r16_state.6)OTE(p29r11_request_run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) ,XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active) XIC(p29r11_index_active) ]OTE(p29r11_index_active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(p29r11_calc_speed_offset,p29_ai_wb_speed-p25_ao_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(p29r11_pid_out,p29r11_calc_speed_offset/p29r11_psn_gain+50);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto Start Sequence]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Configure PID
The tension loadcell feedback is compared to its setpoint in a PID control.
With the PID output at 50%, error is made to be 0
Error is multiplied to the ramped line speed and added to the ramp line speed to calculate the required speed of the drive.
A gain factor is used to dampen the error effect on the drive speed.(P29R10-10)
The larger the number, the smaller the PID error effect.  Initial setting 60]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[TON(p29r11_timer[0],?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29r11_pid_psn_pv);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp,p29r11_pid_psn.SP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tension Error and Load Cell PID - see p29r10.

Rev 20260820]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(p29r11_tension_error,p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp-p29_ai_wdr_lc);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tension Loop Selection - which loop holds web tension

ACCUMULATOR ON   air pressure holds tension.  The carriage position trim
                 drives winder speed, and this PID is parked in manual
                 with its output tracking that trim so the handover is
                 bumpless.

ACCUMULATOR OFF  pressure is zero and the carriage sits on its stop, so
                 nothing pneumatic holds tension.  This PID goes to auto
                 on the winder load cell and trims winder speed - the
                 original pre-accumulator control.

Without this the accumulator work left NOTHING controlling tension when
the accumulator is switched off: speed_offset came only from carriage
position, and with the carriage resting at 0 percent against a 10 percent
park setpoint the trim clamped at its minimum and held the winder at
0.8 x line speed indefinitely.  pid_psn_cv had no consumer at all.

SO is preloaded as offset x gain + 50, the inverse of the offset
calculation, so auto picks up exactly where the trim left off.

Rev 20260904 a38]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p00_wac_enabled)CPT(p29r11_pid_psn.SO,p29r11_speed_offset*p29r11_psn_gain+50);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p00_wac_enabled) ,XIO(p29r11_request_run) ]OTE(p29r11_pid_psn.SWM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)MOV(p29r11_accel_bias,p29r11_pid_psn.BIAS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)MOV(0.0,p29r11_pid_psn.BIAS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)MOV(p21r11_index_kp,p29r11_pid_psn.KP)MOV(p21r11_index_ki,p29r11_pid_psn.KI)MOV(p21r11_index_kd,p29r11_pid_psn.KD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(p29r11_pid_psn.NOBC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If param_psn_gain is too big, fabric will not take up.
If it is too small, you get oscillation.
Big number means small PID error addition to winder speed.
Normal running, need 100.
Turret rotation need 80.
At start of 3" roll, need 40 for about 5 seconds
Use the 3"/6" SS for operator control of faster/slower.
The 3"-6" core switch is used to provide manual pickup speed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[40],p29r11_pid_psn.KP)MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[41],p29r11_pid_psn.KI)MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[42],p29r11_pid_psn.KD)MOV(p29r11_pid_psn.BIAS,p29r11_pid_psn.BIAS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If param_psn_gain is too big, fabric will not take up.
If it is too small, you get oscillation.
Big number means small PID error addition to winder speed.
Normal running, need 100.
Turret rotation need 80.
At start of 3" roll, need 40 for about 5 seconds
Use the 3"/6" SS for operator control of faster/slower.
The 3"-6" core switch is used to provide manual pickup speed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[PID(p29r11_pid_psn,p29r11_pid_psn_pv,0,p29r11_pid_psn_cv,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[org 100]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)MOV(p29r11_param_psn_gain,p29r11_psn_gain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[org 80]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)MOV(p29r11_misc_index_factor,p29r11_psn_gain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Divisor guard - psn_gain

psn_gain divides the PID output twice, and param_psn_gain is adjustable
from the HMI.  Zero faults the processor outright; a very small value is
just as bad without the fault - at 0.1 the speed offset reaches +/-500,
which is a runaway rather than a trim.

Floored at 10, which still allows eight times the normal 80 in
aggressiveness and caps the offset at +/-5.

Placed after both selection rungs so it covers the running gain and the
index gain alike.

Rev 20260904 a40]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(p29r11_psn_gain,10.0)MOV(10.0,p29r11_psn_gain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Position to Winder Speed Trim

See p29r10 for the full description.  Explicit setpoint and gain:

   error = carriage position - p29_param_acc_park_sp
   trim  = error x p29_param_acc_trim_gain, clamped

Rev 20260820 a02]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p00_wac_enabled)MOV(p29_param_acc_park_sp,p29_param_acc_park_sp)CPT(p29r11_acc_pstn_error,p00_wac_position_pct-p29_param_acc_park_sp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Speed Trim - separate gain above and below park

Park sits at 10% of stroke, so the two directions have very different
amounts of travel to work with:

  ABOVE park  90% of stroke.  Gain 0.02 reaches the +0.20 cap at 20%,
              so 100% down to 20% runs flat at 1.20x - the payout
              overspeed - and 20% down to 10% tapers 1.20x to 1.00x.

  BELOW park  10% of stroke.  The same 0.02 could only ever produce
              -0.20 at a bottomed carriage, so trim_min never actually
              clamped anything and the winder could not be slowed by
              more than 20% no matter how empty the accumulator got.

gain_lo 0.05 gives 0.75x at 5% and 0.50x at 0%, with trim_min opened to
-1.00 so the loop can take the winder all the way to a stop.  That is
safe: there is no drive limit slowing down, and the negative-speed block
downstream stops it going into reverse.

Below park the loop is faster - about 5 s versus 13 s above - which is
still well clear of the 25 fpm/s output ramp.  Raise gain_lo on the line
if recovery is too slow, but watch for hunting past about 0.08.

Rev 20260907 a48]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p00_wac_enabled)GRT(p29r11_acc_pstn_error,0)MOV(p29_param_acc_trim_gain,p29_param_acc_trim_gain)CPT(p29r11_speed_offset,p29r11_acc_pstn_error*p29_param_acc_trim_gain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p00_wac_enabled)LEQ(p29r11_acc_pstn_error,0)MOV(p29_param_acc_trim_gain_lo,p29_param_acc_trim_gain_lo)CPT(p29r11_speed_offset,p29r11_acc_pstn_error*p29_param_acc_trim_gain_lo);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p00_wac_enabled)CPT(p29r11_speed_offset,(p29r11_pid_psn_cv-50)/p29r11_psn_gain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Speed Trim Limits

Two different jobs, so two different kinds of limit.

NORMAL RUNNING - fractional.  The trim is drawing the carriage back to
park, and how fast that should happen scales with line speed, so a
fraction is the right shape.  Recovery time then comes out the same at
5 fpm as at 30 fpm.  Limits are param_speed_trim_max / _min.

TURRET INDEX - absolute.  The web path length changes at a rate set by
turret speed and swing radius, in fpm.  It does NOT scale with line
speed.  A fraction is the wrong shape: 0.20 gives 6 fpm of authority at
30 fpm line but only 1 fpm at 5 fpm line, where the disturbance is the
same size.  So during an index the limits become +/- the same absolute
fpm at any line speed:

  trim_hi =  index_trim_fpm / line     ->  winder = line + index_trim_fpm
  trim_lo = -index_trim_fpm / line - 1 ->  winder = -index_trim_fpm

trim_lo goes past -1 on purpose.  Below 1.0 the factor is negative and
the winder reverses, which it must be able to do: at the bottom of the
5-30 fpm range the path lengthens faster than the line feeds.

line_guard floors the divisor at 1.0 fpm.  Line speed reaches 0 whenever
the line is stopped and this rung runs every scan.

Rev 20260825 a26]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p25_ao_selected_speed,p29r11_line_guard);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(p29r11_line_guard,1.0)MOV(1.0,p29r11_line_guard);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r11_index_active)[MOV(p29_param_speed_trim_max,p29r11_trim_hi) ,MOV(p29_param_speed_trim_min,p29r11_trim_lo) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r11_index_active)[CPT(p29r11_trim_hi,p29_param_index_trim_fpm/p29r11_line_guard) ,CPT(p29r11_trim_lo,0-(p29_param_index_trim_fpm/p29r11_line_guard)-1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p00_wac_enabled)sys_Limit_Clamp(p29r11_trim_clamp,p29r11_trim_hi,p29r11_trim_lo,p29r11_speed_offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.10);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp,p29r11_pid_tq.SP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r11_index_active)OTE(p29r11_pid_tq.SWM);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r11_pid_tq.SWM)MOV(p29_ai_wb_torque,p29r11_pid_tq.SO);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.KP,p29r11_pid_tq.KP)MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.KI,p29r11_pid_tq.KI)MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.KD,p29r11_pid_tq.KD)MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.BIAS,p29r11_pid_tq.BIAS)MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.UPD,p29r11_pid_tq.UPD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[PID(p29r11_pid_tq,p29r11_pid_psn_pv,0,p29r11_pid_tq_cv,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29r11_pid_tq.OUT,p29r11_pid_torque);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Faults]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.30);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r11.fault,p29r11.fault_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FAULT)[TON(p29r11_timer_fault[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r11_timer_fault[0].DN) OTL(p29r11.fault.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r11.fault_ack.0)XIC(FAULT)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r11.fault.0) ,OTU(p29r11.fault_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r11.fault,p29r11.fault_ack)OTE(p29r11.unack_fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r11.comment.31);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r11.warning,p29r11.warning_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FAULT)[TON(p29r11_timer_warning[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r11_timer_warning[0].DN) OTL(p29r11.warning.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(FAULT)[OTU(p29r11.warning.0) ,OTU(p29r11.warning_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r11.warning,p29r11.warning_ack)OTE(p29r11.unack_warning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R15_Winder_A_VFD" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[p29r15
This routine is called, continuously, from p29r01 Main while the plc is in Run mode.  All modes and fault reset requests are controlled, here.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()OTE(p29r15.comment.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tag Usage

p29r15.comment (dint)
p29r15.oneshot (dint)
p29r15_timer_xxxx (timer)
p29r15_xxxx (any)
p29r15.fault (dint)
p29r15.warning (dint)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r15.comment.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[60],p29r15_jog_torque_ref)MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[61],p29r15_thread_torque_ref);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r15.comment.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wa_run_position_high_limit,(wa_run_position + param_pos_db))CPT(wa_run_position_low_limit,(wa_run_position - param_pos_db));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[a04 20260820 - LIM operands were reversed on winder A:
LIM(high, test, low).  LIM evaluates the INVERTED range when Low > High,
so turret_in_wda_run_position was true whenever the turret was OUTSIDE
A's run window - backwards.  Winder B was already correct.

The run permissive below was also missing XIC(turret_in_wda_run_position)
entirely, which winder B has, so winder A would run at any turret
position.  Both were introduced together when the inline LIM in the
permissive was refactored into a named bit and only B was completed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(wa_run_position_low_limit,ai_enc_position,wa_run_position_high_limit)OTE(turret_in_wda_run_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder A run permissive

Only three things stop this winder:  its own fault, E-stop, and the
accumulator.  p29r15_drive_ok is XIO(p01r09.fault.0) and EQU(p29r15.fault,0)
- E-stop and own fault, nothing else.

p01r13_permissive_drives has been removed from here.  It carried every VFD
fault on the machine, so a fault anywhere else took the winder's permissive
away - and with it jog and thread, which is exactly when you need the winder
to free stuck fabric.

The turret window stays:  the winder must not run with the turret away from
its run position.  The accumulator has its say through the run request and
through the run request, and through wac_full_stop on the line.  There
is no empty-side stop - empty is the normal running state.  a48

Rev 20260825 a16]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p01r09.fault.0)EQU(p29r15.fault,0)OTE(p29r15_drive_ok);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Run Permissive - Winder A

No turret position compare here.  The interlock that matters - the turret
must not be commanded away from a run position with a winder running - is
enforced once, in p29r20 turret_index_permissive, on the thing that moves.

Duplicating it here as XIC(turret_in_wda_run_position) blocked legitimate
work, because a +/-3 deg window (param_pos_db) is false everywhere except
the run position itself:

  - no jog or thread of the new winder at the load station, which is where
    the leader is attached and has to be wound on
  - no winding the tail off the doffed roll at doff position
  - no accumulator wind-out unless the turret happens to be at run
  - the winder dropped out 0.7 s into a doff index, web still tensioned

Rev 20260825 a23]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)EQU(p29r15.fault,0)OTE(p29r15_run_permissive);]]>
</Text>
