<![CDATA[SYS_ACC_DEC_RAMP(p29r15_torque_ramp,p29r15_selected_torque,p29r15_torque_acc_rate,p29r15_torque_dec_rate,p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,p29r15_ao_torque)MOV(p29r15_ao_torque,p29r15_ao_torque);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Frozen Index Torque - Winder A

Written AFTER the ramp, direct to ao_torque, so it is the last word.
That is how the original ran and it is what the operation depends on.

index_start_torque tracks actual torque continuously while NOT indexing,
so the instant INDEX FWD is pressed the winder is commanded exactly the
torque it was already pulling, and holds it.  Constant torque on a roll
of known radius is constant tension, so the arc cannot disturb the web -
nothing has to compute the geometry.

index_active is a SEAL, cleared only by stopping the winder, so the
freeze holds for the rest of the roll.  As the roll builds, tension falls
as torque/radius - a natural taper of roughly 2 to 10 percent over the
back of the roll depending on web thickness.  That is the existing
winding behaviour and it is deliberately preserved.

It was briefly moved into the selected_torque cascade during the a19
refactor, which let the jog, thread and 90 percent start boost rungs
override it mid-index.  Restored.

Rev 20260831]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r09_torque_mode)XIC(p29r10_index_active)XIC(p29r15_request_run)[GRT(p29_ai_wa_torque,0) MOV(p29r15_index_start_torque,p29r15_ao_torque) ,LEQ(p29_ai_wa_torque,0) MOV(p29r15_jog_torque_ref,p29r15_ao_torque) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Speed Control - Winder A

Five stages, and each winder now owns every one of them.  Winder A and B
are identical rung for rung apart from their own tag names, so both can
jog, thread or wind out at the same time without fighting over a shared
setpoint and a shared ramp.

  1  speed setpoint   fpm - where the speed comes from
  2  own accel/decel ramp
  3  speed factor     dimensionless - which mode is active
  4  one multiply     the ONLY place this winder's speed is calculated
  5  output ramp and clamp

This replaces a cascade of nine writes to p29r15_selected_speed and four to
a shared winder_speed_setpoint, where the last rung to execute won and the
precedence was nowhere stated.  Two faults came straight out of that:

  - the shared MOV(0,winder_speed_setpoint) fired whenever the line was not
    running and no jog was requested, which cancelled the wind out setpoint
    two rungs after it was written.  Wind out never ran.
  - the shared ramp lived inside p29r15, so it executed before p29r16 had
    written the setpoint at all.

Stage 3 is still a priority cascade - that is idiomatic in ladder - but it
is over a dimensionless factor, listed lowest priority first, and it is
trendable online so the active mode can be seen rather than inferred.

Rev 20260825 a18]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r15.comment.7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stage 1 - speed setpoint [fpm]]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,p29r15_speed_setpoint);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
