<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stage 2 - winder A's own ramp.  Rates are shared but the ramp is not, so the two winders no longer share one ramp state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(winder_accel_rate,0)MOV(p29_param_winder_accel_rate,winder_accel_rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(winder_decel_rate,0)MOV(p29_param_winder_decel_rate,winder_decel_rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SYS_ACC_DEC_RAMP(p29r15_acel_decel_ramp,p29r15_speed_setpoint,winder_accel_rate,winder_decel_rate,p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,p29r15_ramped_setpoint)MOV(p29r15_ramped_setpoint,p29r15_ramped_setpoint);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stage 3 - speed factor, LOWEST priority first, last rung to write wins

   0.0                        stopped
   1.0                        jog
   1.5                        thread fwd, or torque mode
   start_speed_factor         running, before state .6 - start slow
   3.0                        boost pushbutton, before state .6
  -1.5                        thread reverse
   1 + p29r10_speed_offset    state .6 - accumulator position trim
   1.0                        line stopped - wind out, trim bypassed
   0.0                        turret going to doff
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0.0,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_request_jog_fwd)MOV(1.0,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="65" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r15_request_thread_fwd) ,XIC(p29r15_request_run) XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ]MOV(1.5,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="66" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_request_run)XIO(p29r09_torque_mode)XIO(p29r15_state.6)MOV(p29_param_start_speed_factor,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="67" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_request_run)XIC(p29_di_wdr_a_start)[XIO(p29r15_state.6) ,XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ]MOV(3.0,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="68" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_request_thread_rev)MOV(-1.5,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="69" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_stop_dwell.DN)XIC(p29r15_state.6)CPT(p29r15_speed_factor,1+p29r10_speed_offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="70" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_request_run)XIO(p01r13_line_running)XIO(p01r13_line_slow_ramp)MOV(1.0,p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="71" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stage 4 - the only place winder A's speed is calculated]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(p29r15_selected_speed,p29r15_ramped_setpoint*p29r15_speed_factor);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="72" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stage 5 - output ramp and clamp]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29r15_fast_accel_rate,p29r15_accel_rate)MOV(p29r15_fast_decel_rate,p29r15_decel_rate)SYS_ACC_DEC_RAMP(p29r15_wdra_accel_decel,p29r15_selected_speed,p29r15_accel_rate,p29r15_decel_rate,p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,p29r15_wdra_ramped_speed)MOV(p29r15_wdra_ramped_speed,p29_ao_wdra_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="73" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Clamp

Loss of run permissive always zeroes the output.

The floor at zero is separate, and no longer unconditional.  It used to
be OR-ed with the permissive test, so ANY negative speed was clamped to
0 - which silently killed thread reverse, since request_thread_rev sets
a speed factor of -1.5 and every bit of it was thrown away at this rung.

It also blocked the reverse the turret index needs at low line speed.

So the floor now applies except where reverse is deliberate: thread
reverse, or an index in progress.  SYS_SPEED_TO_VFD passes a negative
speed straight through - it only guards gear ratio and diameter - so the
drive must be configured for a bipolar speed reference for this to do
anything at the motor.

Rev 20260825 a26]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r15_run_permissive)MOV(0,p29_ao_wdra_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="74" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r15_request_thread_rev)XIO(p29r10_index_active)LES(p29_ao_wdra_selected_speed,0)MOV(0,p29_ao_wdra_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="75" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Faults]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r15.comment.30);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="76" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r15.fault,p29r15.fault_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="77" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_wda_status_word.3)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[0].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="78" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.0)XIO(p29_wda_status_word.3)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r15.fault.0) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="79" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_wda_status_word.0)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[2],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[2].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="80" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.2)XIC(p29_wda_status_word.0)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r15.fault.2) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="81" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_wda_status_word.1)XIO(p29_wda_status_word.9)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[3],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[3].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="82" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.3)[XIC(p29_wda_status_word.9) ,XIO(p29_wda_status_word.1) ]XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r15.fault.3) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="83" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)XIO(p29_di_wa_motor)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[4],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[4].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="84" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.4) XIC(p29_di_wa_motor) XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset) ,XIO(AFI) ][OTU(p29r15.fault.4) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="85" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wa_brake)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[5],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[5].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="86" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.5)XIC(p29_di_wa_brake)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r15.fault.5) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="87" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder Tension High

a04 20260820 - the reset rung used OTL, so it re-latched the fault it was
meant to clear.  p29r15.fault.6 could never be cleared, and because
p29r15_run_permissive and p01r13_permissive_drives both gate on
EQU(p29r15.fault,0), the first tension high event locked out every drive
on the line until a download or an online force.

Now OTU, and following the same pattern as every other fault in this
routine:  acknowledged, condition gone, reset pressed - then clear both
the fault bit and its ack bit so unack_fault clears with it.

Note p29_ai_wdr_lc is a single load cell shared by both winders, so a
tension excursion latches fault.6 on A and B together.  That is correct
for one web, but both need the reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29_param_tension_hi_limit)[TON(p29r15_timer_fault[6],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_fault[6].DN) OTL(p29r15.fault.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="88" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.fault_ack.6)CMP(p29_ai_wdr_lc<(p29_param_tension_hi_limit - 20))XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r15.fault.6) ,OTU(p29r15.fault_ack.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="89" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r15.fault,p29r15.fault_ack)OTE(p29r15.unack_fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="90" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r15.comment.31);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="91" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r15.warning,p29r15.warning_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="92" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_wda_status_word.7)[TON(p29r15_timer_warning[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_warning[0].DN) OTL(p29r15.warning.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="93" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15.warning_ack.0)XIO(p29_wda_status_word.7)[OTU(p29r15.warning.0) ,OTU(p29r15.warning_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="94" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r09_torque_mode)XIC(p29r15_request_run)XIC(p29_wda_vfd.OUT_ENABLED)LES(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29r02_tension_dev_min)[TON(p29r15_timer_warning[1],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_warning[1].DN) OTL(p29r15.warning.1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="95" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ,XIO(p29r15_request_run) ,XIO(p29_wda_vfd.OUT_ENABLED) ,GEQ(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29r02_tension_dev_min) ]OTU(p29r15.warning.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="96" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r09_torque_mode)XIC(p29r15_request_run)XIC(p29_wda_vfd.OUT_ENABLED)GRT(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29r02_tension_dev_max)[TON(p29r15_timer_warning[2],?,?) ,XIC(p29r15_timer_warning[2].DN) OTL(p29r15.warning.2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="97" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ,XIO(p29r15_request_run) ,XIO(p29_wda_vfd.OUT_ENABLED) ,LEQ(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29r02_tension_dev_min) ]OTU(p29r15.warning.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="98" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r15_wdra_active)XIO(turret_auto_index_request)XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)XIO(pb_jog_turret_rev)XIO(turret_in_wda_run_position)OTE(p29r15.warning.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="99" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r15.warning,p29r15.warning_ack)OTE(p29r15.unack_warning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="100" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R16_Winder_B_VFD" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[p29r16
This routine is called, continuously, from p29r01 Main while the plc is in Run mode.  All modes and fault reset requests are controlled, here.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()OTE(p29r16.comment.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tag Usage

p29r16.comment (dint)
p29r16.oneshot (dint)
p29r16_timer_xxxx (timer)
p29r16_xxxx (any)
p29r16.fault (dint)
p29r16.warning (dint)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r16.comment.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[60],p29r16_jog_torque_ref)MOV(p02_real_from_hmi.wdr[61],p29r16_thread_torque_ref);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r16.comment.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wb_run_position_high_limit,(wb_run_position + param_pos_db))CPT(wb_run_position_low_limit,(wb_run_position - param_pos_db));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[a04 20260820 - LIM operands were reversed on winder B:
LIM(high, test, low).  LIM evaluates the INVERTED range when Low > High,
so turret_in_wdb_run_position was true whenever the turret was OUTSIDE
B's run window - backwards.  Winder B was already correct.

The run permissive below was also missing XIC(turret_in_wdb_run_position)
entirely, which winder B has, so winder B would run at any turret
position.  Both were introduced together when the inline LIM in the
permissive was refactored into a named bit and only B was completed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(wb_run_position_low_limit,ai_enc_position,wb_run_position_high_limit)OTE(turret_in_wdb_run_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder B run permissive

Only three things stop this winder:  its own fault, E-stop, and the
accumulator.  p29r16_drive_ok is XIO(p01r09.fault.0) and EQU(p29r16.fault,0)
- E-stop and own fault, nothing else.

p01r13_permissive_drives has been removed from here.  It carried every VFD
fault on the machine, so a fault anywhere else took the winder's permissive
away - and with it jog and thread, which is exactly when you need the winder
to free stuck fabric.

The turret window stays:  the winder must not run with the turret away from
its run position.  The accumulator has its say through the run request and
through the run request, and through wac_full_stop on the line.  There
is no empty-side stop - empty is the normal running state.  a48

Rev 20260825 a16]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p01r09.fault.0)EQU(p29r16.fault,0)OTE(p29r16_drive_ok);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Run Permissive - Winder B

No turret position compare here.  The interlock that matters - the turret
must not be commanded away from a run position with a winder running - is
enforced once, in p29r20 turret_index_permissive, on the thing that moves.

Duplicating it here as XIC(turret_in_wdb_run_position) blocked legitimate
work, because a +/-3 deg window (param_pos_db) is false everywhere except
the run position itself:

  - no jog or thread of the new winder at the load station, which is where
    the leader is attached and has to be wound on
  - no winding the tail off the doffed roll at doff position
  - no accumulator wind-out unless the turret happens to be at run
  - the winder dropped out 0.7 s into a doff index, web still tensioned

Rev 20260825 a23]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)EQU(p29r16.fault,0)OTE(p29r16_run_permissive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Requests]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r16.comment.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29_di_wdr_b_start) ,XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active) ]XIO(p29_di_wdr_b_stop)[OTE(p29r16_wdrb_active) ,OTU(p29r15_wdra_active) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Run Request - Winder B

No turret position term.  The turret indexes whenever the operator asks
for it, and this winder keeps winding wherever the turret happens to be,
until the operator presses the winder stop PB.

Rev 20260825 a28]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16_run_permissive)[XIC(p01r13_line_running) ,XIC(p01r13_line_slow_ramp) ,GRT(p00_wac_position_pct,p29_param_wind_out_stop_pct) ]XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active)OTE(p29r16_request_run);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p01r13_line_running)XIC(p29r09_winder_b_active)[XIC(p01r09_request_line_jog) ,XIC(p29r16_run_permissive) [XIC(p29_di_wdr_jog) XIC(p29r16_zero_speed) ,XIC(p29r16_request_jog_fwd) XIO(p29r16_zero_speed) ] ]OTE(p29r16_request_jog_fwd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16_run_permissive)XIC(p29r09_winder_b_active)XIC(p25r09_mode_thread)[XIC(p25r09_pb_jog_fwd) XIC(p29r16_zero_speed) ,XIC(p29r16_request_thread_fwd) XIO(p29r16_zero_speed) ]OTE(p29r16_request_thread_fwd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16_run_permissive)XIC(p29r09_winder_b_active)XIC(p25r09_mode_thread)[XIC(p25r09_pb_jog_rev) XIC(p29r16_zero_speed) ,XIC(p29r16_request_thread_rev) XIO(p29r16_zero_speed) ]OTE(p29r16_request_thread_rev);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29_param_soak,p29_param_soak);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP(p29_ai_wdr_lc<=(p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp+p29_param_soak))CMP(p29_ai_wdr_lc>=(p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp-p29_param_soak))OTE(p29r16_soak_active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(p29_ao_wdrb_selected_speed,0.1)OTE(p29r16_zero_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r16.comment.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop Dwell - Winder B

The operator presses winder stop.  wdrb_active drops, request_run drops
with it, and that is what raises the fill request and closes the nip in
p31.  The winder must NOT stop in that same instant - it has to keep
tension on the web until the nip has actually gripped it.

TOF: DN stays true while request_run is true AND for the preset after it
drops.  So the fill and nip fire immediately, and the drive stays enabled
and at line speed for the dwell, then ramps down normally.

Rev 20260825 a30]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16_request_run)TOF(p29r16_stop_dwell,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder B drive enable

E-stop clear AND winder B own drive healthy.  Feeds run_permissive
ONLY - never the ACS880 control word.  See the note on the
sys_ACS_FENA21 call below.

Rev 20260906 a45]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r16_stop_dwell.DN) ,XIC(p29r16_request_jog_fwd) ,XIC(p29r16_request_thread_fwd) ,XIC(p29r16_request_thread_rev) ]OTE(p29r16_vfd_start_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder B drive permissive into the ACS880 - E-STOP ONLY

IN_DRIVE_PERMISSIVE is not a general interlock here.  Inside
sys_ACS_FENA21 it drives OFF3_CONTROL, control word bit 2, and an ACS880
does not report RDY_ON until OFF2 and OFF3 are both inactive.

So anything fed here that depends on the drive being ready closes a loop
the drive cannot escape:

  drive not ready -> p29r16.fault.2 latches -> p29r16.fault nonzero
  -> drive_ok false -> OFF3 never set -> drive never becomes ready

a12 replaced drive_estop_ok with p29r16_drive_ok (E-stop AND own faults)
for A/B symmetry, and winder B lost its ready signal permanently.
Reverted to the original.

Winder A is not affected: ABB_PROTOCOL_VFD uses the permissive for
enable_drives, gated separately by DRIVE_NOT_READY_FAULT, and does not
gate the ready report.  Do NOT make these two symmetric.

Winder B own faults still stop it - they break p29r16_request_run via
p29r16_run_permissive.  They must not reach the control word.

Rev 20260906 a45]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p01r09.fault.0)OTE(drive_estop_ok);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[sys_ACS_FENA21(p29_wdb_vfd,vfd_wdb,p29r16_vfd_start_request,p01r09_pb_global_reset,drive_estop_ok);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Sequencer Conditions - Winder B Tension Mode Start Sequence

p29r16_state is a bit-per-state word.  Each transition does MOV(0,state)
then OTL of the new bit, and state.0 is set by the last rung of the group,
so clearing the word also clears state.0 and blocks any further transition
until the next scan - one step per scan.  Same pattern as p01r13_state and
accumulator_state in p31.

  .0  Step gate      set at the end of the group, cleared by every
                     transition.  Not a state.

  .1  Idle/Reset     entered on first scan, from .7, on the winder start
                     PB, in torque mode, or while indexing.
  .2  Start          const_torque_ref (36% small core / 50% large core),
                     speed reference limited to 1.5 x ramped setpoint.
                     torque_start_timer runs while tension is above SP.
  .3  Tension High   load cell > winder_tension_sp -> torque_low_ref
  .4  Tension Low    load cell < winder_tension_sp -> torque_high_ref
  .5  Tension OK     inside the p29r16_tension_ok band
  .6  Run            torque_high_ref, speed = ramped x (1 + speed trim).
                     Gates p29r11_request_run, which in turn is what lets
                     the accumulator pay out - the winder does not draw the
                     accumulator down until tension is established.
  .7  Stopping       run request dropped, returns to .1

  .1 -> .2 -> (.3 | .4 | .5) -> .6 -> .7 -> .1

The direct .2 -> .6 branch is disabled by AFI, so the sequence always
passes through a tension evaluation state before running.

NOTE - p29r16_tension_ok uses a +/-3 lbf band while p29r16_tension_ok on
winder B uses +/-5 lbf.  The two winders are not tuned the same.

Documented 20260820 - logic unchanged.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
