<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Torque Control - Winder B

Same five-stage shape as Speed Control below, and identical to winder B
rung for rung apart from the tag names.

  1  reference sources and the boost timer
  2  selected torque   priority cascade, lowest first
  3  ramp rates
  4  one ramp          the ONLY place p29r16_ao_torque is written

Previously five rungs wrote p29r16_ao_torque DIRECTLY and four wrote
p29r16_selected_torque, with the ramp sitting in the middle of them.  Jog,
thread, state .2 and state .6 all wrote the output directly and were then
overwritten by the ramp, which was dragging the output toward whatever
selected_torque happened to hold - and in tension mode state .6 nothing set
selected_torque at all, so it was a stale value.  The index rung wrote the
output AFTER the ramp and so bypassed it completely.

Every source now writes selected_torque and one ramp produces the output.

BEHAVIOUR CHANGE:  jog, thread, state .2, state .6 and index torque are now
ramped rather than stepped straight onto the output.  Boost is unaffected
in practice - p29r16_torque_boost_acc_rate is 5000, effectively instant.

Rev 20260825 a19]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wdr_b_core_size)MOV(36,p29r16_const_torque_ref);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
