<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Payout Torque

Raises the torque limit so the winder takes the stored web back.

state.6 was REMOVED from this rung.  In torque mode the state machine
is pinned at state.1 - XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) is an unconditioned leg
on the state reset, and the 1 to 2 transition needs torque mode OFF -
so state.6 is unreachable and this rung never fired in torque mode.

The accumulator still ENTERED payout there: winder_running in P31
explicitly allows torque mode.  So it called for payout and the winder
did nothing - nothing emptied the carriage.

request_run plus OUT_Acc_Payout is the correct condition and covers
both modes.  The torque boost rung below still outranks this at start.

Rev 20260907 a47]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16_request_run)XIC(p00_wac.OUT_Acc_Payout)[XIC(p01r13_line_running) ,XIC(p01r13_line_slow_ramp) ]MOV(p29_param_payout_torque,p29r16_selected_torque);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
