<![CDATA[MOV(p29r16_fast_accel_rate,p29r16_accel_rate)MOV(p29r16_fast_decel_rate,p29r16_decel_rate)SYS_ACC_DEC_RAMP(p29r16_wdrb_accel_decel,p29r16_selected_speed,p29r16_accel_rate,p29r16_decel_rate,p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,p29r16_wdrb_ramped_speed)MOV(p29r16_wdrb_ramped_speed,p29_ao_wdrb_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="74" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Clamp

Loss of run permissive always zeroes the output.

The floor at zero is separate, and no longer unconditional.  It used to
be OR-ed with the permissive test, so ANY negative speed was clamped to
0 - which silently killed thread reverse, since request_thread_rev sets
a speed factor of -1.5 and every bit of it was thrown away at this rung.

It also blocked the reverse the turret index needs at low line speed.

So the floor now applies except where reverse is deliberate: thread
reverse, or an index in progress.  SYS_SPEED_TO_VFD passes a negative
speed straight through - it only guards gear ratio and diameter - so the
drive must be configured for a bipolar speed reference for this to do
anything at the motor.

Rev 20260825 a26]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r16_run_permissive)MOV(0,p29_ao_wdrb_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="75" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r16_request_thread_rev)XIO(p29r11_index_active)LES(p29_ao_wdrb_selected_speed,0)MOV(0,p29_ao_wdrb_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
