<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(vfd_wdb.In_DriveStatus_RDY_ON)XIO(vfd_wdb.In_DriveStatus_REMOTE)[TON(p29r16_timer_fault[3],?,?) ,XIC(p29r16_timer_fault[3].DN) OTL(p29r16.fault.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="83" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16.fault_ack.3)[XIC(vfd_wdb.In_DriveStatus_REMOTE) ,XIO(vfd_wdb.In_DriveStatus_RDY_ON) ]XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r16.fault.3) ,OTU(p29r16.fault_ack.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="84" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wb_motor)[TON(p29r16_timer_fault[4],?,?) ,XIC(p29r16_timer_fault[4].DN) OTL(p29r16.fault.4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="85" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16.fault_ack.4)XIC(p29_di_wb_motor)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r16.fault.4) ,OTU(p29r16.fault_ack.4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="86" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wb_brake)[TON(p29r16_timer_fault[5],?,?) ,XIC(p29r16_timer_fault[5].DN) OTL(p29r16.fault.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="87" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16.fault_ack.5)XIC(p29_di_wb_brake)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r16.fault.5) ,OTU(p29r16.fault_ack.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="88" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder Tension High

a04 20260820 - the reset rung used OTL, so it re-latched the fault it was
meant to clear.  p29r16.fault.6 could never be cleared, and because
p29r16_run_permissive and p01r13_permissive_drives both gate on
EQU(p29r16.fault,0), the first tension high event locked out every drive
on the line until a download or an online force.

Now OTU, and following the same pattern as every other fault in this
routine:  acknowledged, condition gone, reset pressed - then clear both
the fault bit and its ack bit so unack_fault clears with it.

Note p29_ai_wdr_lc is a single load cell shared by both winders, so a
tension excursion latches fault.6 on A and B together.  That is correct
for one web, but both need the reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(p29_ai_wdr_lc,p29_param_tension_hi_limit)[TON(p29r16_timer_fault[6],?,?) ,XIC(p29r16_timer_fault[6].DN) OTL(p29r16.fault.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="89" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r16.fault_ack.6)CMP(p29_ai_wdr_lc<(p29_param_tension_hi_limit - 20))XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r16.fault.6) ,OTU(p29r16.fault_ack.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="90" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r16.fault,p29r16.fault_ack)OTE(p29r16.unack_fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="91" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r16.comment.31);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="92" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r16.warning,p29r16.warning_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
