<Routine Name="R17_Winder_A_diameter_calc" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[p29r17
This routine is called, continuously, from p21R01 Main while the plc is in Run mode.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()OTE(p29r17.comment.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tag Usage

p29r17.comment (dint)
p29r17.oneshot (dint)
p29r17_timer_xxxx (timer)
p29r17_xxxx (any)
p29r17.fault (dint)
p29r17a_warnings (dint)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_di_wdr_a_core_size)MOV(3.25,p29r17_selected_core_diameter);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_di_wdr_a_core_size)MOV(6,p29r17_selected_core_diameter);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r09_torque_mode)MOV(p29r09_trq_pos,p29r17_stack_ctrl.POS)MOV(p29r09_trq_len,p29r17_stack_ctrl.LEN)MOV(p29r09_trq_ave_len,p29r17_ave_control.LEN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r09_torque_mode)MOV(p29r09_ten_pos,p29r17_stack_ctrl.POS)MOV(p29r09_ten_len,p29r17_stack_ctrl.LEN)MOV(p29r09_ten_ave_len,p29r17_ave_control.LEN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Requests]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29r18_min_tension,p29r18_min_tension);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Diameter Calculation Enable - payout handling differs by mode

TORQUE MODE  the drive is torque controlled, so RPM is set by the web
             and the roll and is genuine feedback.  Give the formula
             the true web speed and it stays accurate through payout,
             so payout no longer blocks it.

TENSION MODE the winder follows an RPM reference that SYS_SPEED_TO_VFD
             derived from this same diameter, so RPM just echoes the
             command and the result reduces to
                 calc_diam = avg_diam / speed_factor
             It is a trim-settling estimator, not a measurement - which
             is why the transfer below is gated on tension being in
             band.  During payout the trim SATURATES at the +0.25 clamp,
             so it would divide the estimate by 1.25 sample after sample
             and walk the diameter toward zero.  It stays blocked there.


a48 - blocking payout alone was not enough.  ANY non-unity trim walks
the estimate, not just the saturated payout region: the taper from 20%
down to park runs at 1.20x falling to 1.00x and would drag the diameter
down by up to 20% on the way.

The estimator only converges where the trim sits at unity, so that is
now the condition: ABS(speed_offset) below p29_param_diam_trim_band.
The existing tension-in-band gate does not catch this - with the
accumulator holding tension pneumatically it reads in band throughout.

Torque mode bypasses the new test - there the calc is a real
measurement and does not depend on the trim at all.

Rev 20260907 a48]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p00_wac.OUT_Acc_Payout) ,XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ]XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)XIO(p01r13_state.8)XIC(p29r15_request_run)[XIC(p29r15_state.6) ,XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ][XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ,CMP(ABS(p29r10_speed_offset)<p29_param_diam_trim_band) ]CMP(p29_ai_wdr_lc>p29r18_min_tension)GRT(p29_ai_wa_rpm,1)[TON(p29r17_timer[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r17_timer[0].DN) OTE(p29r17_diameter_clac_active) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[True web speed at the winder

Normally the web arrives at line speed.  While the accumulator is
paying out it also delivers acc_payout_fpm on top, and only torque mode
can use the correction - see the note above.

Rev 20260907 a47]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p25_ao_selected_speed,p29r17_web_speed_at_winder);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r09_torque_mode)XIC(p00_wac.OUT_Acc_Payout)CPT(p29r17_web_speed_at_winder,p25_ao_selected_speed+p00_wac_payout_fpm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r15_request_run)XIC(p29_di_wdr_a_reset_core)[MOV(p29r17_selected_core_diameter,p29r17_winder_a_selected_diam_inch) ,MOV(p29r17_winder_a_selected_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_avg_diam_inch) ,MOV(p29r17_winder_a_selected_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch) ,MOV(p29r17_winder_a_selected_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_calc_diam_inch) ,FLL(p29r17_winder_a_selected_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_diam_avg_stack[0],1000) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_diameter_clac_active)XIO(p29r17_timer[1].DN)TON(p29r17_timer[1],?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Divisor guard - winder RPM

Diameter is back-calculated as line speed / winder RPM, so RPM is a
divisor - and it is live feedback from the drive, not a parameter.

diameter_calc_active only proves the winder is REQUESTED to run.  It
does not prove the shaft is turning.  A stall, a drive trip, or a lost
feedback word gives RPM = 0 while the calculation is still enabled,
which faults the processor.

Below 1 RPM the calculation is simply not performed and
calc_diam_inch holds its last good value.  That is better than
flooring the divisor, which would produce a huge diameter that the
LIM(1..30) stack filter would then have to reject.

Rev 20260904 a40]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_diameter_clac_active)GRT(p29_ai_wa_rpm,1.0)CPT(p29r17_winder_a_calc_diam_inch,p29r17_web_speed_at_winder*(12/1)*(1/3.14)*(p29_param_wa_gear_ratio/p29_ai_wa_rpm));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CMP(ABS(p29r10_tension_error)<=p01_param_tension_deviation) ,XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) ]XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)XIC(p29r17_diameter_clac_active)MOV(p29r17_winder_a_calc_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_diameter_clac_active)LES(p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch,p29r17_selected_core_diameter)MOV(p29r17_selected_core_diameter,p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_diameter_clac_active)LIM(1,p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch,30)[XIC(p29r17_stack_ctrl.DN) FFU(p29r17_winder_a_diam_avg_stack[0],p29r17_winder_a_unload,p29r17_stack_ctrl,?,?) ,XIC(p29r17_timer[1].DN) FFL(p29r17_winder_a_actual_diam_inch,p29r17_winder_a_diam_avg_stack[0],p29r17_stack_ctrl,?,?) ,XIC(p29r17_stack_ctrl.DN) AVE(p29r17_winder_a_diam_avg_stack[0],0,p29r17_winder_a_avg_diam_inch,p29r17_ave_control,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_ave_control.ER)OTU(p29r17_ave_control.ER);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17_stack_ctrl.ER)OTU(p29r17_stack_ctrl.ER);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Faults]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.30);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r17.fault,p29r17.fault_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FAULT)[TON(p29r17_timer_fault[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r17_timer_fault[0].DN) OTL(p29r17.fault.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r17.fault_ack.0)XIO(FAULT)XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)[OTU(p29r17.fault.0) ,OTU(p29r17.fault_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r17.fault,p29r17.fault_ack)OTE(p29r17.unack_fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r17.comment.31);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset)MOV(p29r17.warning,p29r17.warning_ack);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FAULT)[TON(p29r17_timer_warning[0],?,?) ,XIC(p29r17_timer_warning[0].DN) OTL(p29r17.warning.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(FAULT)[OTU(p29r17.warning.0) ,OTU(p29r17.warning_ack.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(p29r17.warning,p29r17.warning_ack)OTE(p29r17.unack_warning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
