</Routine>
<Routine Name="R20_Winder_Turret_VFD" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[p29r20
This routine is called, continuously, from p29r01 Main while the plc is in Run mode.  All modes and fault reset requests are controlled, here.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()OTE(p29r20.comment.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tag Usage

p29r20.comment (dint)
p29r20.oneshot (dint)
p29r20_timer_xxxx (timer)
p29r20_xxxx (any)
p29r20.fault (dint)
p29r20.warning (dint)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r20.comment.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r20.comment.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Requests]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(param_doff_position,wa_doff_pos)MOV(wa_run_position,wa_run_position)MOV(param_pos_db,param_pos_db);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wb_doff_pos_tmp,wa_doff_pos+180)MOD(wb_doff_pos_tmp,360,wb_doff_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wb_run_position_tmp,wa_run_position+180)MOD(wb_run_position_tmp,360,wb_run_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CPT(pos_lo_limit_temp,selected_pos+360-param_pos_db) MOD(pos_lo_limit_temp,360,pos_lo_limit) ,CPT(pos_hi_limit_temp,selected_pos+360+param_pos_db) MOD(pos_hi_limit_temp,360,pos_hi_limit) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Sequence
Ramping and Speed Control for entire Letoff Section]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.forward) ,XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.reverse) ]OTE(turret_index_active_last_scan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Original Prox Index Sequence

Restored verbatim from the pre-accumulator program and held as the default.
Hold INDEX FWD, the turret leaves the detent, reaches the next one, dwells,
and index_complete lights the in-position lamp.  Nothing here reads the
encoder.

p29_param_turret_encoder_enable = 0 runs this.  = 1 hands the turret to the
encoder positioning below.  Only request_fwd and request_rev are gated -
the state machine cannot advance past state.1 without them, so it parks
harmlessly when the encoder has the turret.

Rev 20260831]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(p29_ao_wdr_turret_selected_speed,0.1)OTE(p29r20_zero_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable)[XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) XIC(p29r20_zero_speed) ,XIC(p29r20_request_fwd) XIO(p29r20_zero_speed) ]XIO(p29r20.state.6)XIC(p29r20_permissive)OTE(p29r20_request_fwd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable)XIC(p29r20_request_rev)XIO(p29r20_zero_speed)XIC(p29r20_permissive)OTE(p29r20_request_rev);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(S:FS) ,XIC(p29r20.state.8) XIC(p29r20.state.0) ,XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) ][MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.1)XIC(p29r20.state.0)XIC(p29r20_request_fwd)XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)[MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.2)XIC(p29r20.state.0)XIO(p00_io_winder:6:I.15)[MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.3)XIC(p29r20.state.0)XIC(p00_io_winder:6:I.15)[MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.4)XIC(p29r20.state.0)XIC(p29r20_index_move_timer.DN)[MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.5)XIC(p29r20.state.0)XIC(p29r20_zero_speed)XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd)[MOV(0,p29r20.state) ,OTL(p29r20.state.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(S:FS) XIC(p00_io_winder:6:I.15) ,XIC(p29r20.state.5) ,XIC(p29r20_index_complete) ]XIO(p29r20.state.2)OTE(p29r20_index_complete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(p29r20.state.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20.state.4)TON(p29r20_index_move_timer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(p29r20.fault,0)OTE(p29r20_permissive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Turret Index Permissive

The turret indexes when the operator asks, running or not.  Two things
stop it:

  p29r20_permissive   the turret drive itself is healthy
  p29r15/16.fault.6   winder high tension

The swing loads the web: the path from the last fixed roll to the winding
roll lengthens through part of the arc, and if the winder cannot give web
back fast enough the tension climbs.  Stopping the turret removes the
cause; carrying on pulls against it.

Both winders are tested, not just the selected one.  fault.6 latches until
a global reset, so a stale fault on the idle winder will hold the turret
until it is acknowledged - deliberate.

fault.6 = GRT(p29_ai_wdr_lc, p29_param_tension_hi_limit), 20 lbf
hysteresis on the reset.

Rev 20260825 a31]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29r20_permissive)XIO(p29r15.fault.6)XIO(p29r16.fault.6)OTE(turret_index_permissive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder At Run Position - payout interlock export

A active AND A at A run position, OR B active AND B at B run position.
Paired deliberately - it is not enough that some winder is selected and
the turret is at some run position, it must be THAT winder at ITS own.

Exported to controller scope because turret_in_wda/b_run_position are
program scoped to p29 and the payout latch lives in p31.

Evaluated in p29r20, which p29r01 calls after r15 and r16, so the
position bits are current this scan.

Rev 20260829 a33]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p29r15_wdra_active) XIC(turret_in_wda_run_position) ,XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active) XIC(turret_in_wdb_run_position) ]OTE(p29_winder_at_run_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)XIC(turret_index_permissive)[XIC(pb_wa_doff_position) XIC(p29r09_mode_doff_auto) ,XIC(turret_wa_pos_doff_request) XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ][ONS(oneshot.7) MOV(selected_pos,last_selected_position) ,MOV(wa_doff_pos,selected_pos) OTE(turret_wa_pos_doff_request) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)XIC(turret_index_permissive)[XIC(pb_wa_run_position) ,XIC(turret_wa_pos_run_request) XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ][ONS(oneshot.6) MOV(selected_pos,last_selected_position) ,MOV(wa_run_position,selected_pos) OTE(turret_wa_pos_run_request) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)XIC(turret_index_permissive)[XIC(pb_wb_doff_position) XIC(p29r09_mode_doff_auto) ,XIC(turret_wb_pos_doff_request) XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ][ONS(oneshot.5) MOV(selected_pos,last_selected_position) ,MOV(wb_doff_position,selected_pos) OTE(turret_wb_pos_doff_request) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p01r13_permissive_drives)XIC(turret_index_permissive)[XIC(pb_wb_run_position) ,XIC(turret_wb_pos_run_request) XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ][ONS(oneshot.4) MOV(selected_pos,last_selected_position) ,MOV(wb_run_position,selected_pos) OTE(turret_wb_pos_run_request) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Shortest Path to Selected Position

Signed error from where the turret IS to where it is going, wrapped into
-180..+180.  Negative means counter clockwise is the short way round.

  err = selected_pos - ai_enc_position          -360 .. +360
  +540, MOD 360                                     0 .. +360
  -180                                           -180 .. +180

The +540 offset matters: Logix MOD keeps the sign of the dividend, so a
negative error would stay negative and wrap the wrong way.  Adding 540
puts the argument in 180..900, always positive, before the MOD.

Evaluated continuously, not one shot on the request.  The old rung took
SUB(last_selected_position, selected_pos) - the distance between the two
most recent TARGETS, not the distance from where the turret actually is.
After a jog, or an aborted index, that is simply the wrong number.  Live
evaluation also corrects an overshoot instead of driving on round.

Replaces the old 45 deg threshold test and the mode_under HMI override,
which picked direction by rules rather than by which way was shorter.

A run and B run are 180 deg apart, so a run-to-run move is exactly
antipodal and resolves to reverse.  Deterministic, but if that is the
wrong way round the machine, bias one run position by a degree.

Rev 20260825 a25]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(turret_err_raw,selected_pos-ai_enc_position+540)MOD(turret_err_raw,360,turret_err_mod)SUB(turret_err_mod,180,distance_to_move)ABS(distance_to_move,abs_distance_to_move);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(distance_to_move,0)OTE(turret_request_reverse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable)[XIC(turret_wa_pos_run_request) ,XIC(turret_wb_pos_run_request) ,XIC(turret_wa_pos_doff_request) ,XIC(turret_wb_pos_doff_request) ]XIO(turret_auto_index_request)NEQ(ai_enc_position,selected_pos)OTL(turret_auto_index_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GEQ(ai_enc_position,pos_lo_limit) LEQ(ai_enc_position,pos_hi_limit) ,XIO(p01r13_permissive_drives) ,XIO(p29r20_permissive) ,XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) ,XIC(pb_jog_turret_rev) ]OTU(turret_auto_index_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Turret In Position

The turret is in position when winder A or winder B is at its own run
position.  Nothing else counts as in position.

This used to share a rung with the OTU above, which meant losing the drive
permissive, losing the turret drive, or simply jogging all reported the
turret as IN POSITION.  Those conditions belong to the unlatch, not to a
position status, so the two are now separate rungs.

Rev 20260831]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIC(p29r20_index_complete) ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) [XIC(turret_in_wda_run_position) ,XIC(turret_in_wdb_run_position) ] ]OTE(turret_in_position);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIC(p29r20_request_fwd) ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIC(turret_index_permissive) [XIC(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) XIO(pb_jog_turret_rev) ,XIC(turret_auto_index_request) XIO(turret_request_reverse) ] [TON(tmr_fwd_delay,?,?) ,XIC(tmr_fwd_delay.DN) ] ]OTE(p29_do_wdr_turret.forward);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIC(p29r20_request_rev) ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIC(turret_index_permissive) [XIC(pb_jog_turret_rev) XIO(p29_di_wdr_index_fwd) ,XIC(turret_auto_index_request) XIC(turret_request_reverse) ] [TON(tmr_ref_delay,?,?) ,XIC(tmr_ref_delay.DN) ] ]OTE(p29_do_wdr_turret.reverse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) [XIC(p29r20.state.2) ,XIC(p29r20.state.3) ,XIC(p29r20.state.4) ] ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) [XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.forward) ,XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.reverse) ,XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ] ]LEQ(p01_recipe_active.line_speed_sp,10)MOV(p29_param_slow_turret_speed,p29r20_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) [XIC(p29r20.state.2) ,XIC(p29r20.state.3) ,XIC(p29r20.state.4) ] ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) [XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.forward) ,XIC(p29_do_wdr_turret.reverse) ,XIC(turret_auto_index_request) ] ]GRT(p01_recipe_active.line_speed_sp,10)MOV(p29_param_fast_turret_speed,p29r20_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIO(p29r20.state.2) XIO(p29r20.state.3) XIO(p29r20.state.4) ,XIC(p29_param_turret_encoder_enable) XIO(p29_do_wdr_turret.forward) XIO(p29_do_wdr_turret.reverse) XIO(turret_auto_index_request) ]MOV(0,p29r20_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p29r20_fast_accel,p29r20_accel_rate)MOV(p29r20_fast_decel,p29r20_decel_rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SYS_ACC_DEC_RAMP(p29r20_acc_dec_ramp,p29r20_selected_speed,p29r20_accel_rate,p29r20_decel_rate,p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,p29_ao_wdr_turret_selected_speed)MOV(p29_ao_wdr_turret_selected_speed,p29_ao_wdr_turret_selected_speed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
