<Routine Name="R01_Input" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Windup Accumulator
Input]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Analog]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SYS_SCP(add_sys_scp,IN_ai_lpt01,280,27464,0,7620,ai_lpt01_raw)SYS_SCP(add_sys_scp,IN_ai_lpt01,280,27464,100,0,ai_lpt01_pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[LPT Validity - safe fallback

Thirteen rungs in this program now key off ai_pos01_pct_flt:  the winder
speed trim, the outfeed nip, the fill request, the payout latch, the full
stop and the empty alarms.  It is a single point of failure and SYS_SCP
clamps its input, so a failed transmitter does not read as failed - it
reads as a perfectly plausible 0% or 100%.

A broken wire is the dangerous direction:  clamped to 0% the trim goes to
-0.20 and the winder SLOWS, the accumulator fills faster, and wac_full_stop
never trips because position reads empty.  Only di_high_limit would catch
it, at the mechanical stop.

So on A08 the position is forced to the park setpoint.  The trim then
computes zero and the winder tracks line speed, the nip stays open, and no
spurious full or empty is raised.  di_high_limit remains the hard backstop.

ai_lpt01_pct keeps the unfiltered reading for diagnosis on the HMI.

Rev 20260825 a09]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(A08)MOV(p29_param_acc_park_sp,ai_lpt01_pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[VFD]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SYS_SCP(add_sys_scp,p00_io_winder:2:I.Ch6Data,4000,20000,0,200,ai_tension);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(param_sys_filter_lc01,param_sys_filter_lc01)sys_Filter(sys_filter,param_sys_filter_lc01,ai_tension,ai_ten01);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
