</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(pb0.31) ,XIC(p01r09_pb_global_reset) ]OTE(pb_reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Winder Running - is a winder actually taking web?

Mode aware.  In tension mode a winder is only taking web once its start
sequence has reached state .6, which is what p29r10 / p29r11 request_run
already require.  In torque mode the sequencer never leaves state .1, so
those bits are never set and the raw VFD run request has to be used
instead - otherwise winder_running would be permanently false in torque
mode and the accumulator would fill continuously.

Consumed by the payout latch in R22 and the fill request in R21.

Rev 20260820 a02]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(p29r09_torque_mode) [XIC(p29r10_request_run) ,XIC(p29r11_request_run) ] ,XIC(p29r09_torque_mode) [XIC(p29r15_request_run) ,XIC(p29r16_request_run) ] ]OTE(winder_running);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Configuration Parameters]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
