<Routine Name="R04_Data_Out" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Windup Accumulator
Data Out]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Data Out
Data Output to Other Programs]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(A00)OTE(Me.OUT_Not_EStop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Me.OUT_Not_EStop)XIO(A05)XIO(A07)OTE(Me.OUT_Not_Fast_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normal Stop request to the line

wac_empty_stop was REMOVED from this rung.  It is declared but never
written anywhere, so it did nothing - but it sat here waiting for
someone to wire it, and wiring it would stop the line on an empty
accumulator.

Empty is the NORMAL running state for this accumulator.  It parks near
empty on purpose so the full stroke is available to fill during a doff.
Nothing on the empty side may stop or slow the line.  The full side
still does, through wac_full_stop, which is correct.

The empty ALARMS stay - A04 and A06 both require the winders stopped,
and A01 is annunciation only.

Rev 20260907 a48]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(W06)XIO(wac_full_stop)[XIO(pb_acc_on) ,XIO(nip_open_selected) ]OTE(Me.OUT_Not_Normal_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(A06) ,XIC(A04) ]OTE(Me.OUT_Empty);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(A07) ,XIC(A05) ]OTE(Me.OUT_Full);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(accumulator_state.2)OTE(Me.OUT_control_limit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(accumulator_state.6)OTE(Me.OUT_Acc_Payout);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(accumulator_state.3) ,XIC(accumulator_state.4) ]OTE(Me.OUT_Acc_Fill_Request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Pushbuttons from HMI]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,pb0)MOV(0,pb1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
