<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(di_pb_e_stop)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_alarm[0].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[0],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[0].DN) OTL(A00) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(di_pb_e_stop)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A00) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(di_low_limit)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_disc,timer_alarm[1].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[1],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[1].DN) OTL(A01) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(di_low_limit)[OTU(A01) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_alarm[2].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[2],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[2].DN) OTL(A02) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A02) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_alarm[3].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[3],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[3].DN) OTL(A03) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A03) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[A04 - Accumulator Empty with No Winder Running

The old condition was XIO(p29r09_winder_a_active) XIO(p29r09_winder_b_active).
Those two are complementary - a_active is XIC(p29_di_wdr_a) and b_active is
XIO of the same input - so one of them is ALWAYS true and both false is
impossible.  A04 could never latch.

The real test is the run requests.  Empty is normal while a winder is
taking web; empty with NOTHING taking web means the line is feeding into an
accumulator that is already on the bottom, which is worth annunciating.

Gated on the line actually moving, with the standard 3 s dwell, so the
moment at line start - accumulator empty, winder not yet up - does not
trip it.

A04 is ANNUNCIATION ONLY and still needs an acknowledge.  There is
deliberately no empty-side line stop - the accumulator parks near empty
so the full stroke is free to fill during a doff, which makes empty the
normal running state.  Only the FULL side stops the line.  a48

Rev 20260825 a16]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p01r13_line_running) ,XIC(p01r13_line_slow_ramp) ]XIO(p29r15_request_run)XIO(p29r16_request_run)LEQ(ai_lpt01_pct,param_empty_pct)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_alarm[4].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[4],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[4].DN) OTL(A04) OTE(wac_empty_stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(alm_ack[0].4)[GRT(ai_lpt01_pct,param_empty_pct) ,XIC(p29r15_request_run) ,XIC(p29r16_request_run) ][OTU(A04) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Carriage Limit Switches - NORMALLY CLOSED

Both switches are wired normally closed, so a made circuit means the
carriage is clear of the limit.  The alarm is therefore on XIO:

  input TRUE   switch closed, carriage clear
  input FALSE  carriage on the limit, OR a broken wire, OR lost supply

All three fail to the alarm, which is the point of NC.  Previously these
read XIC, so a cut wire read as healthy.

Self clearing - no reset needed once the carriage is back in range.

Rev 20260904 a38]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(di_high_limit)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_disc,timer_alarm[5].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[5],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[5].DN) OTL(A05) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(di_high_limit)[OTU(A05) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(ai_lpt01_pct,param_acc_min_limit)OTE(acc_empty_limit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p29r09_winder_a_active)XIO(p29r09_winder_b_active)XIC(acc_empty_limit)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_1s,timer_alarm[6].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[6],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[6].DN) OTL(A06) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(acc_empty_limit) ,XIC(p29r09_winder_a_active) ,XIC(p29r09_winder_b_active) ][OTU(A06) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(ai_lpt01_pct,param_acc_max_limit)OTE(acc_full_limit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(acc_full_limit)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_disc,timer_alarm[7].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[7],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[7].DN) OTL(A07) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normal Stop Threshold - sized to the line decel

The line decelerates at p01_param_master_decel (2.5 fpm/s), and it keeps
feeding the accumulator all the way down.  Web delivered during the stop is

     V^2 / (120 x decel_rate)   ft

which as a fraction of param_acc_capacity_ft is the stroke that MUST be
left free above the normal stop point, or the accumulator reaches its
mechanical limit before the line is stopped:

      5 fpm    0.08 ft     0.8 % of stroke
     10 fpm    0.33 ft     3.3 %
     15 fpm    0.75 ft     7.5 %
     23 fpm    1.76 ft    17.6 %
     30 fpm    3.00 ft    30.0 %

The old fixed 90% left only 7% of stroke, which is only enough below about
14 fpm.  Above that the line could not stop before the hard limit and the
fast stop always fired instead - which is exactly the steep stop this is
meant to avoid.

A fixed lower threshold would fix 30 fpm but throw away a third of the
accumulator at 5 fpm, where the decel needs almost nothing.  So the reserve
is computed from the present line speed instead, and the threshold floats
with it - the full accumulator is available at creep, the protection is
there at full speed.

Clamped between param_acc_handover_pct and param_acc_max_limit so a bad
speed or decel value can never push it outside the stroke.

Rev 20260825 a10]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(p01_param_master_decel,0)MOV(2.5,p01_param_master_decel);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(param_acc_capacity_ft,0)MOV(10.0,param_acc_capacity_ft);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(acc_decel_reserve_pct,(p01r12_master_ramped_speed*p01r12_master_ramped_speed)/(120*p01_param_master_decel)/param_acc_capacity_ft*100);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(acc_norm_stop_pct,param_acc_max_limit-acc_decel_reserve_pct-param_acc_stop_margin_pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[sys_Limit_Clamp(clamp_norm_stop,param_acc_max_limit,param_acc_handover_pct,acc_norm_stop_pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normal stop latches at the computed threshold and self-clears one
hysteresis band below it.  Routed to Me.OUT_Not_Normal_Stop, so it
requests a controlled line stop and leaves the drives permitted.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(ai_lpt01_pct,acc_norm_stop_pct)OTL(wac_full_stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP(ai_lpt01_pct < (acc_norm_stop_pct-param_acc_stop_hyst_pct))OTU(wac_full_stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(acc_full_limit)[OTU(A07) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].7) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[A08 - Accumulator Position Signal Fault

Three independent tests, any one of which raises A08:

  1  Raw counts outside param_lpt_raw_min / _max.  The SCP scales
     463-18438, so a broken wire reads under that and a short reads over.
     Caught BEFORE the SCP clamps it into a plausible value.

  2  Frozen.  Only armed while the position MUST be changing - filling, or
     paying out.  If it has not moved 0.5% in param_lpt_frozen_ms the
     transducer is stuck.  This catches the failure the range check
     cannot:  a signal that is in band but no longer tracking.

  3  Disagreement with di_high_limit - the discrete says full while the
     analog says it is below the full-stop threshold.  One of them lies.

Not self-clearing.  A sensor fault should be acknowledged deliberately,
unlike the process alarms A05 and A07.

Rev 20260825 a09]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(param_lpt_raw_min,IN_ai_lpt01,param_lpt_raw_max)OTE(lpt_raw_ok);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(request_fill) ,XIC(payout_active) ]OTE(pstn_should_move);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(pstn_should_move) ,CMP(ABS(ai_lpt01_pct-lpt_ref_pct)>0.5) ][MOV(ai_lpt01_pct,lpt_ref_pct) ,RES(timer_lpt_frozen) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pstn_should_move)[MOV(param_lpt_frozen_ms,timer_lpt_frozen.PRE) ,TON(timer_lpt_frozen,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(lpt_raw_ok) ,XIC(timer_lpt_frozen.DN) ,XIO(di_high_limit) LES(ai_lpt01_pct,param_acc_max_limit) ][MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_1s,timer_alarm[8].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[8],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[8].DN) OTL(A08) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(lpt_raw_ok)XIO(timer_lpt_frozen.DN)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A08) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_mcp,timer_alarm[9].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[9],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[9].DN) OTL(A09) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(alm_ack[0].9)XIO(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A09) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].9) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_ol,timer_alarm[10].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[10],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[10].DN) OTL(A10) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(alm_ack[0].10)XIC(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A10) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].10) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_ms,timer_alarm[11].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[11],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[11].DN) OTL(A11) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(alm_ack[0].11)XIO(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A11) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].11) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_alarm[12].PRE) ,TON(timer_alarm[12],?,?) ,XIC(timer_alarm[12].DN) OTL(A12) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(alm_ack[0].12)XIO(AFI)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(A12) ,OTU(alm_ack[0].12) ];]]>
