<Routine Name="R08_Warnings" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Windup Accumulator
Warnings]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(nip_mode_auto) XIC(nip_close_request) ,XIC(nip_mode_close) ]XIO(do_close_nip_sol)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[0].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[0],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[0].DN) OTL(W00) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(nip_mode_auto) XIO(nip_mode_close) ,XIO(nip_close_request) ,XIC(nip_mode_auto) XIC(nip_close_request) XIC(di_ss_close_nip) ][OTU(W00) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(wac_full_stop)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[1].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[1],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[1].DN) OTL(W01) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(wac_full_stop)[OTU(W01) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[W02 - Nip Selector Open with the Accumulator On

The outfeed nip selector is a three position switch:  di_ss_nip_auto,
di_ss_close_nip, and OPEN when neither input is made.  Held open, the
accumulator can drag web back off the winder side during a fill, so the
accumulator cannot do its job.

With the accumulator switched on this blocks Me.OUT_Not_Normal_Stop, which
both prevents a line start and stops a running line.  With the accumulator
off the selector may sit in open freely - the interlock only applies when
the accumulator is meant to be working.

This warning exists because the line simply refusing to start is not enough
for the operator to know why.  It clears itself as soon as either condition
goes away.

Rev 20260825 a12]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_acc_on)XIC(nip_open_selected)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_1s,timer_warning[2].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[2],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[2].DN) OTL(W02) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(pb_acc_on) ,XIO(nip_open_selected) ][OTU(W02) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[3].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[3],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[3].DN) OTL(W03) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AFI)[OTU(W03) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[4].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[4],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[4].DN) OTL(W04) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AFI)[OTU(W04) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(pb_acc_on)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[5].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[5],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[5].DN) OTL(W05) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_acc_on)[OTU(W05) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].5) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_stop_line)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[6].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[6],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[6].DN) OTL(W06) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(wrn_ack[0].6)XIO(pb_stop_line)XIC(pb_reset)[OTU(W06) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AFI)[MOV(p00_lin_timer_pre_0ms,timer_warning[6].PRE) ,TON(timer_warning[7],?,?) ,XIC(timer_warning[7].DN) OTL(W07) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(AFI)[OTU(W07) ,OTU(wrn_ack[0].7) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_reset)MOV(hmi_dint[2],wrn_ack[0])MOV(hmi_dint[3],wrn_ack[1]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Warnings clear automatically, no 
PB_Global_Reset required]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[sys_Acknowledge(add_sys_Acknowledge,wrn_ack[0],hmi_dint[2])sys_Acknowledge(add_sys_Acknowledge,wrn_ack[1],hmi_dint[3]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(hmi_dint[2],0) ,NEQ(hmi_dint[3],0) ]OTE(warning_exists);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(hmi_dint[2],wrn_ack[0]) ,NEQ(hmi_dint[3],wrn_ack[1]) ]OTE(unack_warning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R11_Modes" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Requests]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Modes]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Modes]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(di_ss_nip_auto)OTE(nip_mode_auto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(di_ss_close_nip)OTE(nip_mode_close);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(nip_mode_auto)XIO(nip_mode_close)OTE(nip_open_selected);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R21_Fill_Request" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[WAC
Fill Request and Tension Enable]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fill Request

a02 20260820 - the accumulator position PID has been removed from this
routine.  It regulated carriage position by trimming the carriage
pressure, which is a tension disturbance by definition and conflicted
with the requirement that the accumulator not affect web tension.
Carriage position is now regulated by the proportional position-to-speed
block in p29r10 / p29r11; pressure sets tension only.

Removed:  pid_ctrl_pv / _sp / _cv, the sys_PIDE call, the autotune and
          gain plumbing, PIDE_ten manual mode and manual setpoint, and
          the PID_offset calculation.  The fill pressure bias that
          PID_offset used to supply now falls out of the separate
          vendor fill curve in p31 R22 - see param_press_slope_fill.

Kept declared for HMI back-compat, no longer consumed by any rung:
          PIDE_ten, PIDE_Control, pid_ctrl_pv, pid_ctrl_sp, pid_ctrl_cv,
          PID_offset, pid_mode_manual, use_auto_tune_gains, param_gain,
          param_pid_kp / ki / kd, param_pid_process_type, param_fill_SO,
          param_cv01_manual_sp, param_acc_low_pstn_sp,
          param_low_ctrl_pct, param_high_ctrl_pct.

What remains here is the fill request latch and the tension enable seal.
Routine renamed from R21_Position_PID; call order in R00_Main unchanged.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Tension Enable
Seals in from the HMI enable PB, drops on a system fault or fast stop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(enable_control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fill Request

One rung, plain OTE - NOT a latch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p01r12_zero_line_speed)XIO(p29r15_request_run)XIO(p29r16_request_run)XIO(p00_wac.OUT_Full)OTE(request_fill);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[control_to_empty was driven by the removed position PID.  Held cleared so the HMI status bit does not sit stale at its last value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(control_to_empty);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R22_Fill_Pressure" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Windup Accumulator
Fill Pressure]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(Task,THIS,Rate,task_scan_time_dint)DIV(task_scan_time_dint,1000000,task_scan_time);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Counter pressure
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_acc_on)OTE(p00_wac_enabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_acc_on)MOV(param_counter_prs,ao_prs01);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Pressure Setpoints

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Tension

1 LBF -> 0.2415 PSI   (vendor, emptying)
1 LBF -> 0.2667 PSI   (vendor, filling)

The old 0.0603 here was 1/cylinder area and ignored the 4x from the
2-pass reeving.  See the curve rung below.

Rev 20260829 a32]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Divisor guard - vendor curve slopes

Both slopes are divisors in the pressure calculation below.  They are
not written at runtime, but they are commissioning-editable and a zero
or near-zero would fault the processor or command an absurd pressure.
Same pattern as the param_acc_capacity_ft guard.

Rev 20260904 a40]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(param_press_slope_fill,0.1)MOV(3.75,param_press_slope_fill);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(param_press_slope_empty,0.1)MOV(4.14,param_press_slope_empty);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pressure from Web Tension - vendor curve

C.A. Litzler, measured, excluding friction between parts:

  FILLING    web tension lb = 3.75 x psi - 83
  EMPTYING   web tension lb = 4.14 x psi - 83

inverted for the setpoint:   psi = (tension + 83) / slope

THIS REPLACES THE 0.0603 FACTOR, WHICH WAS WRONG BY A FACTOR OF 4.

0.0603 = 1/16.59, the reciprocal of the combined bore area of the two
3.25 in cylinders.  That converts cylinder FORCE to pressure - but web
tension is not cylinder force.  The carriage is reeved 2 passes, and
each pass puts two spans of web on the carriage, so the cylinders carry
4 x T:

  psi = 4T/16.59 = 0.2411 T      vs vendor 1/4.14 = 0.2415 T

The old factor commanded a quarter of the pressure needed.  At 1 PLI the
tare masked it (34.6 vs 35.3 psi); at 2.5 PLI it was 40.3 psi against a
required 58.1 - the accumulator would have held about a third of the
tension asked for, and worse the higher the setpoint.

The 83 lbf offset is the carriage: 83 x 16.59/4 = 344 lb, consistent with
the mechanical note that the carriage must fall under its own weight.

Rev 20260829 a32]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wac_calc_tension_pressure,p01_recipe_active.winder_tension_sp+param_press_offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Filling and Emptying Pressures

Two curves, not one pressure plus a bias.  Filling needs more pressure
than emptying for the same web tension, and the gap is not constant -
3.7 psi at 1 PLI, 6.0 psi at 2.5 PLI.  A fixed param_fill_bias_psi could
not represent that, so it is gone.

  wac_tension_pressure  = (tension + 83) / 4.14 + trim    emptying, hold
  filling_pressure      = (tension + 83) / 3.75 + trim    fill request

param_tare_pressure is now a TRIM, starting at 0.  The vendor curve
already carries the carriage weight in the 83 lbf offset, and is stated
to exclude friction between parts.  Any standing offset found at install
- seal drag, guide friction - goes here.  It is no longer the whole
intercept, so do NOT set it to 30.8.

Check against the vendor table at install:

  PLI   tension lb   fill psi   empty psi
  1.0        63        38.9       35.3
  1.5        94.5      47.3       42.9
  2.0       126        55.7       50.5
  2.5       157.5      64.1       58.1

Rev 20260829 a32]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(wac_tension_pressure,wac_calc_tension_pressure/param_press_slope_empty+param_tare_pressure);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Pressure Select

DESIGN INTENT:  the accumulator is transparent to web tension.  The web
sees the same tension with the accumulator in the loop as it would with
the accumulator bypassed, in every state where the web is flowing through
to the winder.

The cylinders are a constant-force device.  Pressure sets web tension; it
does NOT set carriage position.  Carriage position is set by the mass
balance between what the line feeds in and what the winder draws out.

Rungs are in order of increasing priority - the last rung to write
selected_pressure wins:

  1  Normal run                 wac_tension_pressure
  2  Payout                     wac_tension_pressure
  3  Fill request               filling_pressure  (steeper fill curve)
  4  Fault, or line not moving  wac_tension_pressure

1, 2 and 4 are all the same pressure, and that is the point - nothing
about accumulator state changes web tension.  During payout the carriage
descends because the winder is overspeeding and drawing web out faster
than the line feeds it in, not because pressure was reduced.

The position PID offset is NO LONGER added to the running pressure.  Any
position trim on the pressure is a tension disturbance by definition, so
the carriage is left to float.  PID_offset now reaches the web only
through the fill bias in rung 3, where the exit nip is closed and the
winder is isolated from the accumulator.

Superseded, no longer used:  payout_pressure (fixed 29 psi),
param_holding_pressure (fixed 14 psi), tension_pressure (fixed 35 psi).

Rev 20260820]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(request_fill)XIO(payout_active)MOV(wac_tension_pressure,selected_pressure);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(filling_pressure,wac_calc_tension_pressure/param_press_slope_fill+param_tare_pressure);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Payout Status and Carriage Position Publish

The winder speed trim is now a strict proportional function of carriage
position, done with a scaling block in p29r10 / p29r11:

        0%  ->  -0.20      winder at 0.80 x line, accumulator refills
       10%  ->   0.00      park, in balance
       20%  ->  +0.20      winder at 1.20 x line, drawing down
   above 20% ->  +0.20      saturated - this IS the payout overspeed

Because that curve is continuous there is no payout-to-running handover
to sequence and no cross-fade.  The accumulator seeks 10% on its own,
which also removes the position drift that a purely tension-transparent
accumulator would otherwise show over a long run.

p00_wac_position_pct is the filtered carriage position published to p29.
P31 scans after P29 so p29 reads it one scan old - 10 ms on a carriage
that moves slowly, which is not significant.

payout_active / accumulator_state.6 / Me.OUT_Acc_Payout are retained as
STATUS ONLY - HMI indication and the pressure select rungs below.  They
no longer gate any speed logic.  Latch is at park + 2% so that a short
doff which only part-fills still shows payout; unlatch at park, with
wac_nearly_empty kept as a backstop.

Rev 20260820]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(ai_lpt01_pct,p00_wac_position_pct);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Payout Rate - web speed the carriage is adding

The winder diameter calculation back-solves diameter from line speed
and winder RPM, and it assumes the web speed AT THE WINDER equals line
speed.  During payout that is false - the carriage is releasing stored
web, so the winder pulls line speed PLUS the payout rate.

Rate comes straight from the carriage: stored length is position x
capacity, and its rate of change is the web being released.

Guards, in order:
  - scan time floored so the divide cannot fault
  - clamped to [0, param_payout_rate_max]; negative means FILLING and
    must not be fed to the diameter calculation
  - first order filter, since this is a derivative of an analog
  - forced to zero whenever payout is not active, so nothing leaks

Rev 20260907 a47]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(acc_length_ft,p00_wac_position_pct/100*param_acc_capacity_ft);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(p01r02_plc_scan_time_in_sec,acc_rate_dt);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(acc_rate_dt,0.001)MOV(0.001,acc_rate_dt);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(acc_rate_fpm_raw,(acc_length_last_ft-acc_length_ft)/acc_rate_dt*60);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(acc_length_ft,acc_length_last_ft);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(acc_rate_fpm_raw,param_payout_rate_max)MOV(param_payout_rate_max,acc_rate_fpm_raw);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(acc_rate_fpm_raw,0.0)MOV(0.0,acc_rate_fpm_raw);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(acc_payout_fpm,acc_payout_fpm+(acc_rate_fpm_raw-acc_payout_fpm)*param_rate_filter);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p00_wac.OUT_Acc_Payout)MOV(0.0,acc_payout_fpm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(acc_payout_fpm,p00_wac_payout_fpm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Payout Activation

Payout only runs into a winder that can actually take the web:

  winder A active AND turret at winder A run position, OR
  winder B active AND turret at winder B run position

via p29_winder_at_run_position.  Without it the accumulator would pay
out while the turret is mid-index or parked at doff, with the selected
winder nowhere near the web path.

Losing the interlock also drops payout, not just blocks it starting -
the turret can be jogged away underneath an active payout.

Rev 20260829 a33]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(request_fill)CMP(ai_lpt01_pct>(param_acc_handover_pct+2))XIC(winder_running)XIC(p29_winder_at_run_position)[OTL(payout_active) ,OTL(accumulator_state.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LEQ(ai_lpt01_pct,param_acc_handover_pct) ,XIO(p29_winder_at_run_position) ][OTU(payout_active) ,OTU(accumulator_state.6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(payout_active)MOV(wac_tension_pressure,selected_pressure);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(request_fill) CMP(ai_lpt01_pct<= param_acc_handover_pct+param_acc_handover_band_pct) ,XIO(p29r15_request_run) XIC(p29r15_wdra_active) ,XIO(p29r16_request_run) XIC(p29r16_wdrb_active) ][MOV(wac_tension_pressure,selected_pressure) ,OTE(accum_tension_pressure_on) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(request_fill)[MOV(filling_pressure,selected_pressure) ,OTE(accum_filling_on) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Hold the accumulator in position

Applied on a fault, or when the line is not moving and neither winder is
running.  Holding pressure is now the calculated tare + tension pressure so
the carriage stays where it is instead of drifting down - it was a fixed
param_holding_pressure of 14 psi, well below the carriage tare.

A fill request is not overridden here unless there is a fault, and
p01r13_line_slow_ramp is now included in the line-not-moving test.

param_holding_pressure is no longer used.

Rev 20260820]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(p01r09.fault,0) ,XIO(request_fill) XIO(p01r13_line_running) XIO(p01r13_line_slow_ramp) XIO(p29r15_request_run) XIO(p29r16_request_run) ][MOV(wac_tension_pressure,selected_pressure) ,OTE(accum_holding_pressure_on) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Accumulator Pressure Accel Decel Ramp

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pb_acc_on)sys_Ramp(add_sys_ramp,param_accel_rate,param_decel_rate,task_scan_time,ao_prs02,selected_pressure)MOV(selected_pressure,ao_prs02);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(do_carriage_lift_sol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(pb_acc_on)MOV(14,selected_pressure)MOV(0,ao_prs01)MOV(14,ao_prs02);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R31_Nip_Roll" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[WAC
Nip Roll]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Notes:
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR()NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nip Control]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nip Open Dwell

The fill request clears the moment a winder is started again.  The nip
must not open on that instant - the winder needs 2 s at payout overspeed
to pick the web up and establish tension first, or the nip lets go into
slack web.

E-stop bypasses the dwell and opens the nip immediately.

Rev 20260825 a30]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(request_fill)TON(nip_open_dwell,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nip closes only while the accumulator is filling

The outfeed nip is a one way roll - material pulls out toward the winder
with it closed but cannot roll back.  Its only job is to stop the
accumulator dragging web back off the winder side while it fills, so that
is the only condition that closes it.

Open on E-stop.  Me.OUT_Not_EStop is A00 only, so this forces the nip open
regardless of the fill request and regardless of the manual close selector.
The solenoid rung also drops on any p01r09 fault, so E-stop is covered
twice - deliberately.

Previously opened on accumulator level above param_acc_min_limit.  That
left it open during the fill, which is the one time it needs to be shut.

No open delay - the level-based version needed one, this does not.
timer_nip_open_delay is left declared and unused.

Rev 20260825 a12]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(nip_open_dwell.DN) ,XIO(Me.OUT_Not_EStop) ]OTE(nip_auto_open_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(nip_mode_auto) XIO(nip_auto_open_request) ,XIC(nip_mode_close) ]OTE(nip_close_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(nip_mode_auto)XIO(nip_close_request)OTE(nip_open_request);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(nip_close_request) ONS(oneshot.0) ,XIC(do_close_nip_sol) ]EQU(p01r09.fault,0)XIC(nip_close_request)XIO(nip_open_request)OTE(do_close_nip_sol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(W00) XIC(p00_FlashBit_1Sec) ,XIC(nip_mode_auto) XIO(W00) ,XIC(do_close_nip_sol) ,XIC(p00_pb_lamp_test) ]OTE(do_nip_illuminated_ss);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
